            <ArticleTitle>Carbapenemase VCC-1-Producing Vibrio cholerae in Coastal Waters of Germany.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1735-1737</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2310.161625</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During antimicrobial drug resistance testing for Vibrio spp. from coastal waters of Germany, we identified 4 nontoxigenic, carbapenem-resistant V. cholerae isolates. We used whole-genome sequencing to identify the carbapenemase gene blaVCC-1. In addition, a molecular survey showed that more blaVCC-1-harboring isolates are present in coastal waters of Germany.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
